System Logic

The system continuously polls all sensors and performs automatic decisions in real time.

Example Operations
If engine temperature exceeds 90°C:
Cooling fan turns ON
Fault code logged to EEPROM
If ambient light becomes low:
Headlights automatically turn ON
If obstacle distance becomes less than 10 cm:
Buzzer alarm activates
Parking warning displayed on LCD
If smoke is detected:
Emergency alarm activates
Fault code stored in EEPROM
If unauthorized touch is detected:
Security alarm activates
Tamper fault logged
Diagnostic Fault Logging

The system stores faults as Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) similar to real automotive ECUs.

Example Fault Codes
P001 → Obstacle detected
P002 → High engine temperature
P005 → Smoke detected
P006 → Tamper attempt detected

Stored data can later be retrieved and displayed on the LCD for diagnostics.

